WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.567
The US State

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.835
Department confirmed that a US

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.770
Marine veteran was killed

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.672
on the outskirts of Back Mount Ukraine.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.973
26 year old Cooper

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.608
Harris Andrews was likely killed

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.810
by a mortar on April 19

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.212
while helping citizens

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.480
evacuate the embattled city,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.614
according to his mother.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.648
She says his body still

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.583
has not been recovered

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.317
because of the fierce

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.852
ongoing fighting there.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:19.319
CNN's Nick

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.353
Paton Walsh reports for us

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.654
now from southeastern Ukraine.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:22.355
As the world awaits

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.724
a major new phase in the war

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.894
and in the battle in parliament,

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.798
It was hard to get much uglier.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.766
But each dawn

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.701
still, the battle for parliament

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.202
grinds on.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.805
Ukraine Monday said it had pushed

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.440
Russian forces back

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.110
who had abandoned positions in months

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.211
of agonizing

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.814
fighting for about a football field.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.416
Every day Say analysts

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:53.186
leaving

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.155
political standing

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.490
and Russian injured,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.659
the soldiers here said abandoned

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.096
assault Then there was a guy laying there

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.165
in the reeds, he says, yelling,

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.566
Guys, come and help me.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.934
For three days,

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.670
only 100 yards from the Russians.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.838
Also emerging, too.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.572
On this,

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.907
the road of life,

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.909
the last way in and out of the city.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.078
News of the death of Cooper

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.813
Harris Andrew's age

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.582
26 A former US Marine and firefighter

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.150
from Cleveland, Ohio,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.452
who felt compelled

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.954
to join Ukraine's fight.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.857
Cooper wanted to correct things

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.125
We had a lot of

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.893
conversations about fashion.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.861
I used Cooper.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.528
So that means

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.496
just going over there

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.432
to drive an ambulance

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:42.602
and that is now

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.671
you just don't believe in stuff you like.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.306
Do something about it.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.742
I was let's make a picture for a history

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.112
Here he is near the front line in January

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.880
as part of the Foreign Legion,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.349
described as ideological to the core,

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.817
an anti-authoritarian.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.486
His body has yet to be recovered.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:00.553
From Back Mount

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.422
as the fighting is too intense.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.656
His mother recalled

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.525
the last time they spoke.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.459
I asked Cooper

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.061
because I'm like Hoover's mom.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:08.228
Like,

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.629
is there anything I can try

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.297
and get to you or send in?

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.799
Cooper said. Yes,

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.370
Can you send me

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.573
hot sauce and tufts

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.512
So I have like a thousand

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.846
chopsticks in my house

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.748
because I was trying to get chopsticks

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.482
for everyone.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.850
I figured people would stop this,

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.153
and I have all these little packets of

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.322
hot sauce

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:40.260
that I was going to send to Cooper.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.395
Over the past weeks, graphic battle

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.830
footage has emerged

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.931
showing what it's like

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:45.698
when Russians

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.968
get into a Ukrainian trench network here.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.271
A soldier races into cover.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.006
Sure, that was funny.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:56.142
But soon a shell hit

00:02:57.277 --> 00:03:00.013
Oh, they are all miraculously okay.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.782
But the attack has started

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.552
You watch

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.086
and you see a Russian approach

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.955
and throw a grenade

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.027
He misses

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.430
And they go on to shoot down

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.499
Russians advancing meters from them.

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.171
Shells continue to land.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.473
The attack persists for over 10 minutes.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.310
But the brutal fight for Buckland

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.277
goes on and on

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.584
So what is happening around back moot?

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.551
A matter of weeks ago,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.220
the Russians seem to be signaling

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.521
that they were in the ascendant.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.156
And then we had the Russian head

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.090
of the foreign mercenary

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:44.791
group, Evgeny

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.526
Prigozhin, over the weekend suggests

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.061
they're running out of artillery shells

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.062
and might have to pull back.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.463
And now Ukraine says

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.531
they're on the front foot

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:52.966
and Russians are abandoning

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.100
their positions.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.568
The city is becoming

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.770
a kind of signaling game for both sides,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.072
says project strength,

00:03:59.072 --> 00:03:59.906
and then possibly

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.541
drag each other's forces in.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.443
It is something of a sideshow

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.878
despite the extraordinary loss of life.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.813
One indication

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:07.680
from John Kirby,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.581
the National Security

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.916
Council spokesperson,

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:10.516
is they might

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.653
Russia have lost 100,000 troops

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.622
since December, mostly fighting for back

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.724
movements, casualties dead and wounded.

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.591
The realize though

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.125
right now

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:19.792
on the larger

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.727
counter offensive

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:23.029
most likely not around back much

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.398
but in the south of Ukraine Jake.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:25.632
All right.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:26.733
Nick Paton Walsh

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.568
live for us in Ukraine, thank you.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.702
Stay safe.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.169
Joining us now

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.005
to take a step back on the war

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.641
in Ukraine, take a 30,000 foot view.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.409
The Atlantic magazine's

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.710
editor in chief, Jeffrey Goldberg,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.911
he and staff writer.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.846
And Applebaum

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.514
wrote the June EDITION's cover

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.316
story entitled The Case

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.485
for the Total Liberation of Ukraine.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:47.820
And you can read that online today.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.888
Jeffrey, thanks for being here.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.355
Appreciate it.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.457
You write that a victory for Ukraine

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.226
can be easily defined.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.360
It would mean sovereignty,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.528
safety, justice,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:58.998
but getting there not so easy to define.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.801
You spoke with Zelensky at length twice

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:03.670
Where does his

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.371
optimism

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.473
about a victory, about a path to this?

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.942
This this proposal,

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.010
where does it come from?

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.212
His optimism comes in part

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:16.783
from the serial underestimation

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.951
of the entire world

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.820
about Ukraine's capabilities.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.089
I mean, you know, we talk about Obama.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.159
Russia bogged down in this tiny

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:28.394
town, relatively small town

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.698
for months and months and months.

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:33.032
If you recall, think back

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.534
14, 15 months ago,

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.169
we thought Ukraine was going to be

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:36.969
wiped out,

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.572
wiped off the map in a matter of days.

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.241
And you know, we were in Kiev.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.010
I was in Kiev last year here and there

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.244
this year.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.679
The change is remarkable,

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.014
even though it's under periodic

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.649
rocket attack.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:50.450
You know,

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.317
there is no

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.352
existential threat

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.954
to most of the country anymore.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:55.655
And what

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:56.255
what I mean

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.056
by all of that

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:57.890
is that

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.992
we have underestimated their resolve.

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.661
They're capabilities,

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:02.962
their desire to win.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:05.264
Russia has no morale whatsoever.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.066
Ukrainians are all morale.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:10.503
Our argument, of course, is that Ukraine,

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.739
the fighters of Ukraine can do this

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:14.941
without foreign troops, without U.S.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.175
troops, NATO's troops.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.778
But what they can't do without is

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.146
the support

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.315
is the the American materiel,

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:23.483
the weapons systems,

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:25.184
the most advanced weapons systems.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.420
This is the year to do it.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.621
Obviously, the U.S.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:29.255
has provided

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.057
a tremendous amount of material

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:32.392
to the Ukraine, know more than anyone.

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:34.560
By force. By far. By far.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.828
But with the argument

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.430
now is

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.599
if they have just a little bit more help

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:41.701
and a lot more concentration of help,

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:42.568
they'll actually be able

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.537
to change the lines on the battlefield.

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:45.705
You also write about the looming

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:46.806
counter offensive.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:47.440
You write, quote,

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.341
Ukrainians are waiting

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.042
for the counter-offensive of Ukraine.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.611
Europeans east and west

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:52.845
are waiting for the counter offensive.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:53.980
Central Asians are waiting for

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:54.947
the counteroffensive.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:55.114
Well,

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.716
the Russians, Venezuelans, Iranians

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:57.450
and others around the world

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.184
whose dictatorships

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.552
are propped up by the Russians,

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.720
they are all waiting

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.088
for the counteroffensive to this spring,

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:02.889
this summer.

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:04.223
This autumn, Ukraine gets a chance

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:07.293
to alter geopolitics for a generation,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:10.163
and so does the United States.

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.031
Do you think President Biden

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:12.932
agrees with that?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.569
I think President Biden

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:18.604
feels that very much

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.473
I think he has a pretty acute

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:22.041
understanding of this

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:24.110
and travesty of the U.S. role here.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:24.710
The U.S.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:24.911
is the

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.746
leader to use a somewhat archaic term,

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:29.248
but no longer archaic the U.S.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:30.783
is the leader of the free world.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.151
Right. Ukraine.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.754
Ukraine can keep itself from losing.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.322
However, we define losing. Right.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.356
That's what they proved to us

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.091
in those opening days of the war

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.960
when they didn't get steamrolled. Right.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.962
Ukraine cannot win

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.997
without the United States behind it.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:45.965
100%.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:46.999
The danger here,

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:47.200
I mean,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:47.867
obviously, there's a

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:48.835
there's a range of views

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:50.236
inside the Biden administration.

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:51.904
I think everyone's heart.

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.339
Certainly the president's heart

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:54.974
is with the people of Ukraine

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.476
and the president of Ukraine.

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.144
I think there are differing

00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.178
views about

00:07:59.178 --> 00:07:59.946
whether the Ukrainians

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:01.614
can actually push

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:04.150
Russia out of all of its territory,

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.384
all the territory that it's holding.

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.019
Right. Including Crimea.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:08.321
The hardest one, obviously.

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:09.889
And obviously an interesting debate over

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.091
whether they can achieve that.

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:13.359
The main fear,

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:15.261
of course, is that the US is trying

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:15.862
and Biden has done

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:17.129
a very good job of doing this

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.264
caliber shading

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:18.831
to try

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.132
to calibrating this

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.534
so that they don't provoke Russia

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:23.569
into doing something insane.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:24.237
And the worry,

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:24.871
of course, is that

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:25.404
the Russians

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:27.406
will use a nuclear weapon in some form

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.040
or fashion. Yeah.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:28.674
President Biden,

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.042
when I interviewed him last fall,

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:31.644
he seemed to suggest that

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:33.646
Putin was halfway there in terms of the

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:35.481
the stability.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:36.482
But I wanted

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:37.783
the interesting part of your story.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:38.551
You met with Ukrainians

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:39.118
who are working in

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.654
these privately financed drone workshops,

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:43.623
and you saw how drones that were used

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:44.790
for wedding photography

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.359
before the war were had been transformed

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:47.460
into lethal weapons

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.762
that could even destroy a tank.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:52.398
Is the ingenuity of the Ukrainian people

00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:54.400
one of its most secret weapon?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.535
This is this is

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.637
this is why they don't need troops

00:08:57.637 --> 00:08:58.604
from the United States.

00:08:58.604 --> 00:09:00.373
They don't need that much advice

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:01.374
from the United States.

00:09:01.374 --> 00:09:03.175
They need they need material help.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:03.876
The these

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:06.279
these drone factories are amazing.

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:07.113
The defense

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.447
minister of Ukraine told us something

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:09.782
that was fascinating.

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:11.551
He said when the war started,

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.151
people thought

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.019
that this was going to be a war

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.820
between a large Soviet army

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.322
and a small Soviet army.

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:18.024
But what they didn't understand

00:09:18.024 --> 00:09:18.190
was that

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.692
Ukraine had changed over the last

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:20.493
20 or 30 years

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:22.395
and was now a Western army,

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.597
an innovative or flattened hierarchy.

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:25.631
The Russians are still fighting

00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:26.465
like Soviets

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:27.500
The Ukrainians are fighting

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.002
like American Special Forces.

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:30.403
The drone

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:31.904
workshops are just a case in point.

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:33.573
The Russians in Bermuda and elsewhere

00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:35.575
are just trying to go home alive. Right.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:36.943
They don't care

00:09:36.943 --> 00:09:38.144
The morale is extremely low.

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:39.845
Ukrainians are fighting for their cities.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:40.580
They're building

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.581
I mean, they're using

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:42.148
they're using

00:09:42.148 --> 00:09:42.882
literally wedding

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:44.250
drones are using model

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.885
airplanes as drones

00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:46.652
and they're doing this

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.154
in hundreds of different locations

00:09:48.154 --> 00:09:49.589
on their own initiative.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:51.090
It's totally fascinating to watch.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.992
The story is the case

00:09:52.992 --> 00:09:54.794
for the Total Liberation of Ukraine.

00:09:54.794 --> 00:09:55.695
Written by

00:09:55.695 --> 00:09:57.430
Jeffrey End and Applebaum

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.131
on the Atlantic.com right now.

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:00.066
Thanks so much for being here.

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:01.133
Thank you. Amazing reporting.

